Trees generating near chunk boundaries had trunks placed at edge positions (0 or 15), causing leaves extending beyond chunk limits to be clipped, resulting in visually incomplete trees.

## Changes

- **Boundary constraint**: Tree trunks now only generate at positions 1-14 (inclusive) on both X and Z axes within each chunk
- **Scope**: Applied to all tree generation calls (regular trees, big trees, and biome-specific variants)

```rust
// Only generate trees if trunk is at least 1 block away from chunk edges.
// This prevents trees from looking incomplete when their leaves would extend
// beyond chunk boundaries and get clipped.
let is_valid_tree_position = dx >= 1 && dx < CHUNK_SIZE - 1 && dz >= 1 && dz < CHUNK_SIZE - 1;

if is_valid_tree_position {
    let tree_chance = rand::random::<f32>();
    match biome_type {
        BiomeType::Forest => { /* tree generation */ }
        // ...
    }
}
```

Since tree leaves extend up to 2 blocks from the trunk center, a 1-block margin reduces but doesn't eliminate clipping. Full prevention would require 2-block margins or cross-chunk generation queuing.

